    "title": "Five Delco communities say yes to regional ambulance service - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Editorials ,\n1 days ago Five municipalities recently officially voted to establish the Municipal Emergency Medical Services Authority of Delaware County (MEMSA) in a regional effort to solve the county’s ambulance service crisis. The new public authority creates a joint regional body to fund and manage advanced life support (ALS) ambulance coverage across Nether Providence Township, Upper Providence Township, Rose Valley Borough, Rutledge Borough, and Swarthmore Borough. Read full article\n5",
